<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Tia approves $50 mln bond program.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Tia approves $50 mln bond program.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine supermarket chain Tia SA said Wednesday it has approved a $50 million global negotiable bond program.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement to the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange the issues may be placed abroad or in Argentina and may include foreign currency issues as well as the peso.</p>
<p>Tia did not say when it is likely to launch the first</p>
<p>issue, but it added that it will seek approval for the program</p>
<p>from the National Securities Commission.</p>
<p>Dutch bank ING will structure the program and</p>
<p>will underwrite the issues.</p>
<p>    -- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 3180668</p>
</text>
